  "boundary": "Two RF3/fsync shards in one isolated Docker network namespace, 256 rows per shard for the final matrix; 2 CPU and 1536 MiB cgroup limits. Correctness and fault-inclusive drill timings only; no independent-host failure-domain, online-overhead, PB-capacity or production-RTO claim.",
  "failure_analysis": {
    "cb-second.json": "Development missing optional membership field; fixed by returning explicit null.",
    "cb-third.json": "Development nonexistent digest.hex API; replaced with hex encoding of the actual digest bytes.",
    "cb-full-lua.json": "Concurrent trial passed offline logical audit but restored readiness timed out; election/replication timeout logs retained. Root cause not established.",
    "cb-full-vinyl-native.json": "Concurrent trial lost writable leader before local-space control; root cause not established.",
    "cb-final-memtx-lua.json": "Serial earlier trial lost writable leader before membership publication; timeout logs retained. Final fixture observes readiness before that mutation without resending any mutation. Root cause of transient role loss remains unproven.",
    "cb-physical-regression.json": "The invocation reduced payload from the fixture default 4096 to 1024 bytes. The resulting 281688-byte backup completed too close to its 1-second lease-expiry threshold, so the expected-expiry assertion failed. The unchanged fixture passed at its documented default payload; this is an input-dependent control, not a backup code fix."
  },
  "development_boundary": "Exploratory results are not final acceptance evidence. Per-file hashes bind each recorded input; working-tree labels do not identify immutable commits. cb-full-lua and cb-full-vinyl-native overlapped. Original failed records and logs are preserved separately from later passes.",
